Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on Proposition 5.10 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2412.13392).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2412_13392.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2412.13392/gen_2412_13392.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2412.13392/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2412.13392/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2412.13392/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2412.13392/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2412.13392/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass:

- Planted certificates: 16/16
- Structure-aware guesses: 0/250,000
- Four attacks: each 0/8
- Reference matching algorithm: 8/8, approximately 1.19 million operations
- Compact structural route: 8/8, 233 operations
- Canonical-key transformations and diversity: all 20/20
- Answer: 216 characters, 75 atoms

The external hardening verdict remains unavailable. The supplied OpenRouter key returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for all bare, structural-hint, and placebo calls, leaving zero scored oracle attempts. The error transcripts are retained honestly; the family needs those three harness runs repeated after refreshing the key before it is release-ready.
